  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.62,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_tolerance",
      "components": ["R34"],
      "pins": ["R34.1", "R34.2", "U5.23"],
      "nets": ["/BRA_{pH}", "GND"],
      "observed": "R34 (U5's BRA current-sense resistor, 110 mΩ) is specified with a 10% tolerance: its instance description reads '110 mOhms ±10% 0.333W, 1/3W Chip Resistor 0805 (2012 Metric) Current Sense Thin Film' and carries an explicit field 'Tolerance = 10%'. Its own library part is 'RES 110mΩ ±1% 1/4W 0805 Susumu' (PN RL1220S-R11-F, the 'F' suffix = ±1%), and the five sibling sense resistors R30–R33 and R35 all keep the ±1% description with no Tolerance override.",
      "expected": "All six TMC2209 current-sense resistors (R30–R35, 110 mΩ per the spec's §2 TMC2209 row) should be the same ±1% Susumu RL1220S-R11-F part, as the library part and the other five instances specify, so each driver's chopper current regulation and stallGuard back-EMF thresholds are set accurately.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"R34\") (value \"110mΩ\") ... (description \"110 mOhms ±10% 0.333W, 1/3W Chip Resistor 0805 (2012 Metric) Current Sense Thin Film\") ... (field (name \"Tolerance\") \"10%\") ... (libsource (lib \"Coert-Vonk\") (part \"RES 110mΩ ±1% 1/4W 0805 Susumu\")"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"R30\") (value \"110mΩ\") ... (description \"110 mOhms ±1% 0.333W, 1/3W Chip Resistor 0805 (2012 Metric) Current Sense Thin Film\")"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "each with its own current-sense resistor pair (R30–R35, 110 mΩ)"}
      ],
      "impact": "The A-coil sense resistor of the pH-Down dosing driver U5 can be off by ±10% instead of ±1%, so U5's regulated motor current (and any stall/jam threshold derived from it) deviates up to ~10% from the value set by the R24/R25 VREF divider and from the other two pumps — a peristaltic pump running at the wrong current, giving dosing-rate error and inconsistent stall behavior versus Nutrient-A/B.",
      "confidence": 0.62
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The r2 netlist matches the specification's architecture (TPS62933/AZ1117 rails, ADM3260 isolated pH/EC channels, three TMC2209 drivers with correct coil, UART, STEP/EN and VREF wiring, float-switch interlocks, and the documented known limitations), but R34 — one of the six matched 110 mΩ current-sense resistors — is recorded as a ±10% part against its own ±1% library part and its five ±1% siblings, a sourcing/assembly deviation that skews the pH-Down pump's current regulation. This is the only supported anomaly."
}

